.TH CYLK 1 "2026-10-19" "cylk 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cylk \- temporarily disable the built-in laptop keyboard for cleaning
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cylk
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cylk
grabs the internal evdev keyboard of a laptop so that the keys can be cleaned
while the computer is running. The touchpad and external keyboards keep
working.
.PP
The keyboard is released automatically when the selected duration ends, when
the Stop button is pressed, when Esc is held for two seconds, when the window
is closed, when the app exits, or when logind reports a screen lock, suspend,
or inactive session. A small privileged helper, launched on demand through
.BR pkexec (1),
performs only the evdev grab and does not read key events.
.PP
A three-second countdown is shown before the grab. The default duration is 60
seconds and can be set to 30, 60, or 120 seconds.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
Print the detected keyboards and exit. Each line contains the classification
(internal or external), evdev path, device name, detection score, bus, and
hardware path.
.TP
.BR \-d " " \fIPATH\fR ", " \-\-device= \fIPATH\fR
Use the evdev device at
.IR PATH .
The path can also be a udev hardware identifier such as
.IR platform-i8042-serio-0 .
.TP
.B \-\-duration=\fISECONDS\fR
Set the cleaning duration. Valid values are 30, 60, and 120.
.TP
.B \-\-demo=\fISTATE\fR
Preview the interface without grabbing a keyboard. Valid states are
.IR idle ,
.IR countdown ,
.IR cleaning ,
and
.IR done .
.TP
.B \-\-quit-after=\fISECONDS\fR
Close the application automatically after the given number of seconds. This
option is intended for testing and screenshots.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options.
.SH SAFETY
The privileged helper checks that the requested path is a char device in
/dev/input with a full keyboard capability bitmap. It waits for all keys to be
released, takes an exclusive
.B EVIOCGRAB
grab, drops privileges to the invoking user, sets
.BR PR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS ,
and clears the dumpable flag.
.PP
The helper enforces its own maximum duration of the selected duration plus five
seconds. Closing its standard input or its file descriptor releases the grab;
the kernel also releases an evdev grab when the process exits, so the keyboard
is restored even if the graphical interface crashes.
.PP
The application does not read, log, or transmit key presses. It polls the key
state only to detect the held-Esc release gesture.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/clean-your-lap-keyboard/settings.ini
Persisted duration and manually selected keyboard.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/io.github.julcal008.CleanYourLapKeyboard.policy
Polkit policy for the privileged helper.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/clean-your-lap-keyboard/cylk-helper
Privileged helper. The exact path depends on the distribution and installation
prefix.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the available keyboards:
.PP
.nf
    cylk --list
.fi
.PP
Clean the internal keyboard for two minutes, using an explicit device:
.PP
.nf
    cylk --device /dev/input/event4 --duration 120
.fi
.PP
Preview the cleaning screen without touching the keyboard:
.PP
.nf
    cylk --demo=cleaning
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR loginctl (1),
.BR udevadm (8)
.PP
